MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Kanban workers (scratch cwd), cron jobs (no workdir) and Desktop chats opened in project folders never saw
~/AGENTS.md: core only loads AGENTS.md along the git-root -> cwd chain. New config key (default [] = upstream):
each readable file loads for every session of the profile, in the context tier before the project chain, as
its own '<path> (global)' section with the same scan + truncation caps. Content identical to a loaded project
file is loaded once (cwd == ~). Cron's identity-only mode (skip_context_files + load_soul_identity) loads the
global files too. Missing/unreadable paths are skipped with an info log line. /context manifest lists the rows
(loaded/duplicate/missing).
